  "body": "Branch `fn-paged-kv` `f23b5ab5` on `main` `d1018b31`. Part of #781's follow-ups (other families on the core pool).\n\n## What this changes\n\nThe seven `flashnext_attn.cu` kernels that touch a stream's caches now take a `Pg` argument: an int page table, the\nelements in a page, and the positions in a page. They are `fn_attn_prep(_media)`, `fn_qsa_pool(_media)`,\n`fn_qsa_scores` and `fn_attn_chunks(_ahead)`. `pg_at()` finds each row:\n\n- with no table, it is the old expression;\n- with a table, it is the start of the page that holds the position, plus the row inside that page.\n\nA page of n positions holds, for each attention layer:\n\n- the keys, values and indexer keys of its n positions;\n- the pooled rows of their n / 4 blocks.\n\nA cache pointer is its layer's part of page 0 (layout in `cuda_pages.zig`). Only addresses change; no sum changes\norder. So paged caches give the contiguous bytes at any page size that holds whole blocks.\n\n- `TF_FLASHNEXT_KV_PAGE_TEST=n` reads each stream's caches through a reversed table of n-position pages. It is for\n  checks only.\n- `fn_attn_chunks` looks up a key's row once per tile (`key_at` in shared memory, beside `key_ids`), and the pool kernel\n  once per block of four; the contiguous path pays one uniform branch.\n- Prompt-cache saves and restores copy page runs in the contiguous layout, so kept states move between the two forms.\n- A captured Triton set refuses a page table.\n\n## Receipt\n\n- Environment: TensorFold `main` `d1018b31` plus this branch; one DGX Spark (GB10, sm_121, CUDA 13.0, nvcc 13.0.88);\n  `nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP4-Local@b9ce18a6`.\n- Kernel contract: `tf-cuda-test flashnext-pages`, also run inside `kernel-contract`.\n  - Six cases: cached lengths up to 9,000; pages of 16, 48, 128, 256 and 512 positions; two streams shuffled through\n    one arena.\n  - Paged output equals contiguous over three repeats for: queries, indexer queries, block scores, dense and sparse\n    attention rows, the stores, and the pooled rows.\n  - Attention rows stay within a float64 bound, and the guards are intact.\n  - Controls are red: a swapped table over placed pages, and a planted row.\n  - Gate 5: new nvcc 13.0 records for the five kernels whose register counts moved. All seven pass live. The 13.2\n    override set still needs regenerating with nvcc 13.2, which is not on this box.\n- Served, greedy, `--parallel 4 --context 40960 --no-drafts`, ABAB against `main` (c=1 tok/s code/chat, TTFT):\n\n  | arm | replies | c=1 | ~8k | 31k |\n  | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n  | main, run 1 / 2 | - | 23.46/23.40, 23.38/23.48 | 6.04-7.00 s | 25.67 / 26.01 s |\n  | this, contiguous, run 1 / 2 | equal (3 chats, three ~8k, one 31k) | 23.51/23.49, 23.55/23.44 | 5.97-6.91 s | 25.64 / 25.74 s |\n  | this, page test 16 | equal | 23.56/23.38 | 6.05-6.90 s | 26.08 s |\n\n  The page test's first version (one page-table lookup per 16-byte load) cost +3-4 % at 31k; one lookup per key per tile\n  removes that.\n- Gates with MTP drafts, page test 16, compared with contiguous:\n  - drafted == plain: 8/8;\n  - concurrent == solo: 8/8;\n  - resumed == fresh: yes, with 7,147 tokens restored into pages;\n  - every output equals contiguous.\n- Tests: full `zig build test -Dnvcc=/usr/local/cuda/bin/nvcc` exit 0, `zig fmt --check` clean, lean check 0 new\n  findings; `kernel-contract`: 85/85 kernels pass gates 1-4, 7 controls red (exit 1 only from `main`'s 877 limit\n  problems).\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- **Off by default:** only the check switch `TF_FLASHNEXT_KV_PAGE_TEST` uses pages here. The pool itself is the stacked follow-up, #1170.\n- **Gate-5 records:** the nvcc 13.2 override set for the five kernels whose registers moved isn't regenerated, because there is no nvcc 13.2 here. The 13.0 records are new.\n- **Captured Triton sets** refuse a page table.\n- **Overlap:** #1113 pages Flash Next KV to host RAM for its EXL3 path. That is a different mechanism, but the same family, so expect textual overlap. No conflict with #1143, #1147, #1155 or #1164.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Every token still goes through the lane rounds.\n- [x] Drafted output equals `\"draft\": false`, a resumed prompt equals a fresh one, and concurrent equals solo. All\n      three were measured on the page test.\n- [x] No precision traded for speed. The bits do not change.\n- [x] New and changed kernels are registered with the kernel contract, with red controls.\n- [x] Prompt processing is no slower than the last release (contiguous within main's spread).\n- [x] Platforms: CUDA on GB10 (sm_121), one rank; other SMs through recorded compiles; no Metal change.\n- [x] Comments are one line. No measurements or history in the source (lean check 0 new).\n- [x] No personal data, machine names, internal hosts or local paths. No AI attribution lines.\n",
